WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.720
So we now have a situation and we're going
to have time to have a sort of bigger conversation

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.260
about this as we get closer and closer to
Joe Biden's inauguration.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:17.690
But we have a situation here where Donald
Trump now has cost the Republican Party everything

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.590
Trump has cost the Republican Party everything
he could have cost them.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.480
Donald Trump cost the Republican Party, the
House in the twenty eighteen midterms.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.860
Donald Trump cost the Republican Party, the
Senate.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:36.480
In the 2012 election, Donald Trump caused
himself to be a one term president, now putting

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.010
the Republican Party out of the Oval Office
just 13 days from now.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:47.650
Donald Trump has cost the Republican Party
global shame and embarrassment and has ruined

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:49.860
the careers of many, many people.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.380
And so we're seeing Republicans start to turn
on Donald Trump.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.120
Donald Trump denounced his own vice president,
Mike Pence, yesterday in the middle of the

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.120
Capitol Hill.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.920
Riots that he incited himself.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.879
We saw Mick Mulvaney, who I learned during
the break, went from being Trump's chief of

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.820
staff to like an envoy to, I think, Ireland.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:09.820
And he resigned.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.140
And there are thoughts that there may be more
resignations.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.860
There are thoughts that there are reports
that some cabinet members are thinking about

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.180
invoking the 25th Amendment to try to remove
Donald Trump.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:24.130
So from the point of view of blame and from
the point of view of holding people accountable,

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.020
none of these Repub oh, sorry, I hit my mic.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.020
I'm so excited.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.369
None of these Republicans deserve to now be
praised and to be given a blank slate because

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:35.939
with 13 days to go, they said this is too
much for me.

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:43.990
This segment is not about praising the moral
Republicans who after three years and 11 and

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:47.900
a half months, are now saying this is too
much for me.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:53.400
This is not about that, but this is about
what does the future of the Republican Party

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.400
look like.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.189
And in particular, after this week, not only
did Donald Trump incite a seditious riot in

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:04.400
the capital, but he also oversaw the two people
he endorsed.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.340
Carly Lefler and David Perdue lose their Senate
seats as incumbent Republicans.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.720
To Democratic challengers Raphael Warnock
and John Asaph.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.629
You are starting to see Republicans bail and
you start to see these reports like we saw

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:24.120
in the week about Republicans privately furious
at Trump over what happened in Georgia and

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.329
Republicans privately furious that Trump put
them in a position to have to either support

00:02:29.329 --> 00:02:35.519
bogus claims of voter fraud or have to denounce
Donald Trump, essentially, and risk.

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:40.129
Being on the receiving end of Trump's anger,
these Republicans are complete fools and they

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:43.230
deserve none of our pity whatsoever.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:48.209
But the question does become what happens
in the next two years and in the next four

00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:49.209
years?

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:53.909
And what I care about is, is there an opportunity
for Joe Biden to get things done?

00:02:53.909 --> 00:02:57.470
Because Donald Trump has so debased and destroyed
the Republican Party, the Republican Party

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:01.829
will rebuild and they may even do well in
2022.

00:03:01.829 --> 00:03:07.249
I think it's more likely they do well in the
House than the Senate because of the cohort

00:03:07.249 --> 00:03:10.819
of Senate elections that are taking place
in 2022.

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:17.349
But the point is, I care about progress and
Joe Biden is going to come in in 13 days and

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:19.760
he'll start doing things that he can do via
executive order.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.519
And that's going to be fine.

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:24.879
And then we don't know if Joe Biden is going
to get any Supreme Court picks, but if he

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:27.069
does, we'll deal with that when it comes to
it.

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:32.140
But the real question is going to be from
the big legislative agenda, from the big policy

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.239
agenda, what can Joe Biden get done?

00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:41.150
We've said before these Republicans are going
to be the total obstructionists that we've

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.790
seen them be in the past.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:48.099
They are going to get in the way of Joe Biden
doing almost anything with control of the

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:49.099
Senate.

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:53.579
Now 50 50 with Kamala Harris as the tie breaking
vote and continued control of the House with

00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:58.719
total government control by Democrats, there
is now a real possibility that some of the

00:03:58.719 --> 00:04:00.189
big agenda items can be done.

00:04:00.189 --> 00:04:05.959
Can we do a big infrastructure, green energy
deal?

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:11.559
Can we get the public option done and reduce
the Medicare age and make the other changes

00:04:11.559 --> 00:04:15.750
that that Joe Biden has lobbied for or campaigned
on?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.729
What is Joe Biden going to be able to do in
terms of foreign policy and foreign relations

00:04:19.729 --> 00:04:20.729
and rebuilding?

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:25.360
And the questions around policy are the same
ones.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.211
But with much of the Republican Party now
distancing from Trump, the question is, is

00:04:30.211 --> 00:04:36.970
there anything that can be done that will
get a few Republicans to be allies, even if

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:42.759
just for the next two years that give Joe
Biden the opportunity to really get some important

00:04:42.759 --> 00:04:43.759
things done?

00:04:43.759 --> 00:04:48.430
There are moral questions we could have an
ethical debate about whether, you know, wouldn't

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:54.490
that risk rehabilitating the reputation of
some of these Republicans who don't deserve

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.990
that reputation to be OK?

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:58.099
We can have that debate.

00:04:58.099 --> 00:05:02.169
But at the end of the day, Trump had this
list of things he was going to do and he failed

00:05:02.169 --> 00:05:03.169
to do most of them.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.169
And that's great.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:06.440
He was going to do his horrible health care
plan.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:07.440
He failed.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.720
He was going to build a wall and he failed
a lot of the good things he promised.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:14.340
He also failed on 100 million vaccines by
the end of 2020.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.580
Israeli-Palestinian peace.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.620
You know, the list of things that it would
have been nice to do that he failed on is

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.650
also there.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:21.650
And that's what it is.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.639
The presidency is ending.

00:05:23.639 --> 00:05:25.319
What can Joe Biden get done?

00:05:25.319 --> 00:05:31.439
And is there any politically strategic way
that these last two weeks during which Trump

00:05:31.439 --> 00:05:35.240
denounces his own VP and Republicans start
to distance?

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.479
These are still terrible people.

00:05:37.479 --> 00:05:44.729
But from the totally pragmatic perspective,
can this be leveraged in any way to get something

00:05:44.729 --> 00:05:47.659
done that we really need to get done in this
country?

00:05:47.659 --> 00:05:49.780
We'll leave that question there and we'll
pick it up next week.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.570
